    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nwhen i `:ls` and there's multiple results a `hit-enter` prompt appears and `Press ENTER or type command to continue` shows.\n\nwhen using `@:` to repeat last command-line it should repeat the `:ls` command and show the prompt again, but with mini.clue enabed the prompt doesn't show\n\n### Reproduction\n\nmini.clue config\n\n```lua\nreturn {\n  'echasnovski/mini.clue',\n  opts = {}\n}\n```\n\n1 - `:echo \"one\\ntwo\"` (a prompt shows)\n2 - `@:` (the prompt doesn't show)",
    "closed_at": "2025-02-23T12:48:12Z",
