            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nYes, I can reproduce. This is a result of 'mini.clue' [overriding the `@` and `Q`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/b612a069d1fe99300da43629e0e9c7a1a9b0acda/doc/mini-clue.txt#L93-L94) to have them execute macros without 'mini.clue' triggers active (as they might interfere sometimes). Unfortunately, I don't think there is anything 'mini.clue' can do here as the mapping for `@` *has* to be implemented the way it is implemented now (i.e. has `nowait=true` to be executed immediately to not have to create all `@a`/`@b`/etc mappings and use `vim.fn.getcharstr()` to get the next character as register id).\n\nA cleaner approach (without custom mappings) requires new autocommand events in Neovim which I suggested adding 1.5 years ago (neovim/neovim#24565), but it got stalled without answers from maintainers.\n\nSo I am afraid I am going to close this as a Neovim upstream issue.\n\n------\n\nOne workaround around this is to create custom mapping for `'@'` that executes registers built-in way (before or after 'mini.clue', it doesn't matter since somewhat recently). With something like `vim.keymap.set('n', '@', '@')`. The downside is that all macros will be executed with 'mini.clue' triggers active, which can have unwanted side effects.",
