            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> thank you for the detailed response, as for the workaround would `vim.keymap.set('n', '@:', '@:')` also cause the side effects?\n\nIt would not work as 'mini.clue' makes its `'@'` mapping with the `nowait = true` flag. It means that it stops waiting for another key form user as soon as `@` is typed. I am not quite sure why it was added (probably because 'mini.clue' triggers themselves use `nowait = true` flag), but I am sure there was a reason. The 'mini.clue' module overall is a bit hacky as it has to deal with Neovim's built-in key query process which itself comes form 30+ years of Vim development.",
